    <string name="sec_hint">Minutes a day on one part of an app — WhatsApp\'s Updates and channels, CapCut\'s templates — while the rest of the app stays open. Counted only while that part is on the screen and the screen is on; at midnight the count starts again. Needs the accessibility service below.</string>
    <string name="sec_service_label">Reader\'s Detox — sections</string>
    <string name="sec_service_desc">Sees which part of WhatsApp or CapCut is on the screen, to count the minutes a parent allowed on it and leave it once they are spent. Reads no message and keeps nothing of the screens.</string>
    <string name="sec_service_on">accessibility service: running</string>
    <string name="sec_service_off">accessibility service: off</string>
    <string name="sec_service_hint">tap to switch it on in the settings. It lets the app see which part of WhatsApp or CapCut is on the screen; no message is read.</string>
    <string name="sec_service_off_since">accessibility service: off since %1$s</string>
